  "before_any_accepted_sample": [
    "Startup: sample_start records console FD, queries kern.bootsessionuuid and mach_timebase_info, validates values, emits/flushes one SAMPLE_READY before readiness notification watch and HID device creation. No proc scan/pipe/fork/tool invocation.",
    "Idle: sample_poll tests static child=-1 and immediately returns. No extra sleep, poll syscall or timestamp read occurs on this branch. Existing loop delay100ms and lifetime7200s checks remain.",
    "Input: new SAMPLE prefix test precedes old OPEN/HID demux. Ordinary lines return0; ordinary OPEN/HID additionally check sample_busy=false. Invalid SAMPLE-prefixed lines may count toward existing rejection limit.",
    "Global replay capacity40\u219242, preserving HID32/OPEN8 and adding SAMPLE2. Existing same-ID replay behavior unchanged.",
    "Cleanup: sample_close returns immediately without a child. No sample-related signal or tool work occurs before accepted SAMPLE.",
    "Backend object bytes,77-byte descriptor and two entitlement dictionary are identical; no new dependent dylib or static initializer. Main stack prologue remains96 saved-register bytes plus512 local bytes.",
    "Mach-O text10436\u219215204 bytes, BSS1964\u21922264, fullfile70848\u219288944; addresses/stubs and static-data layout change, so startup/cache/scheduling timing can change without an explicit display change."
  ],
